  "gaps": [
    "FIN 490 Finance Capstone has no printed credit value; 3 credits is inferred from the 51-credit major total minus the 48 credits printed for the other 16 major courses.",
    "Block totals (33 Global Campus Foundations + 51 major + 39 electives = 123) exceed the 120-credit total because 3 major credits (ECO 203, marked *) may also satisfy Global Campus Foundations requirements; the capture does not say which Foundations course ECO 203 replaces.",
    "The Global Campus Foundations courses listed are the general bachelor's 'standard' sequence and 'Courses may be substituted'; the capture does not give the Foundations category structure or substitution rules for this program.",
    "The capture does not explicitly name the credit unit as semester credits; 'semester' is assumed for the credit system.",
    "Residency: a minimum of 30 credits must be completed at the University as a matriculated student; no specific course is identified as institution-only.",
    "Upper-division: a minimum of 30 upper-division credits, including 18 upper-division credits in the major; course levels counting as upper-division are not defined in the capture.",
    "GEN 101 (and GEN 104 for students transferring fewer than 30 credits) is scheduled and counts toward elective credits; the remaining elective content is unspecified.",
    "A Quantitative Reasoning requirement must be met before BUS 401 and BUS 308; how it is satisfied is not stated in the capture.",
    "FIN 490 must be taken last in the program.",
    "Minimum cumulative GPA of 2.00 in all coursework attempted at the University is required."
  ],
